<!-- Deep Dives -->
<section class="section" aria-label="Deep Dive">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="section-label-pill">Deep Dive</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Same meetings, different homes</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Otter.ai and EnviousWispr both turn meetings into transcripts. Where that happens, and what else each app does, is what separates them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="deep-dive-grid">
      <div class="deep-dive-card reveal">
        <div class="deep-dive-icon">🎯</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-title">Your Mac or the cloud, plus dictation</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-body">
          <p>Otter.ai records meetings. It joins your Zoom, Meet, or Teams call, captures everything, identifies speakers, and produces a searchable transcript after the fact. The output lives inside Otter's app. It is a meeting productivity tool.</p>
          <p>EnviousWispr puts text where you type, in real time. Hold a keybind, speak, release. Text appears in your email draft, Slack message, code editor, or Google Doc. There is no separate transcript window, no copy-pasting, no switching tabs. It replaces your keyboard for moments when speaking is faster than typing.</p>
          <p>EnviousWispr also records meetings, on your Mac, with EnviousMeet. It records your microphone and, on macOS 14.2 or later, the sound your Mac plays. No bot joins. After the meeting you get a transcript with who said what, your notes, and an optional summary.</p>
          <p>If your team shares meeting notes, wants a bot in every call, or searches across months of meetings, Otter is the right tool. If you want meetings transcribed on your own Mac, and dictation in every app, EnviousWispr does both for free.</p>
          <div class="deep-dive-detail">
            <strong>Key difference:</strong> Otter keeps your meetings in its cloud for your team. EnviousWispr keeps them on your Mac, and also puts text where you type.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="deep-dive-card reveal">
        <div class="deep-dive-icon">🛡️</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-title">Privacy: on-device vs cloud</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-body">
          <p>Otter.ai uploads all audio to its cloud servers. Transcripts are stored online and processed by Otter's AI for summaries, action items, and search indexing. Your voice data lives on their infrastructure.</p>
          <p>EnviousWispr processes audio entirely on your Mac's Apple Silicon chip. Nothing is uploaded. Dictation audio is cleared after transcription; meeting audio stays on your Mac until you delete it. If you choose a cloud AI provider, only text is sent (the transcript, plus your notes for a meeting summary). OpenAI, Gemini and Claude receive it under your own key; a hosted Ollama model sends it to Ollama's servers.</p>
          <p>Cloud processing is what gives Otter team sharing and search across every meeting. EnviousWispr transcribes meetings and labels speakers on your Mac, so the audio never leaves it. For personal messages, medical notes, legal correspondence, or anything sensitive, on-device processing means your words never leave your control.</p>
          <div class="deep-dive-detail">
            <strong>The tradeoff:</strong> Otter's cloud approach enables team sharing and cross-meeting search. EnviousWispr's local approach keeps meeting audio and transcripts on your Mac, with speakers labelled after the meeting, not live.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

