<section class="section" aria-label="Frequently Asked Questions">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="section-label-pill">FAQ</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Common questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Is EnviousWispr an Otter.ai alternative?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">For many people, yes. Both record and transcribe meetings, in different ways. Otter.ai is a cloud service: it can join calls as a bot, keeps transcripts online, and adds team sharing and search across meetings. EnviousWispr records meetings on your Mac with EnviousMeet, with no bot and no audio upload, and writes a transcript with who said what, your notes and an optional summary. It also types by voice into any app on your Mac, which Otter does not.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Can I use EnviousWispr to transcribe meetings?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">Yes. EnviousMeet, built into EnviousWispr, records a call or an in-person meeting on your Mac. No bot joins. It records your microphone and, on macOS 14.2 or later, the sound your Mac plays, so the other people on a call are included. After the meeting you get a transcript with who said what, your notes, and an optional summary. Otter.ai is the better choice if your team needs to share transcripts or search across every meeting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Is there a free dictation alternative to Otter.ai?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">Yes. If what you actually need is dictation (typing by speaking into emails, Slack, documents), EnviousWispr does that for free with no account, no subscription, and no usage limits. See the <a href="/blog/getting-started-enviouswispr-under-2-minutes/" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline;">getting started guide</a>. Otter's free tier limits you to 300 minutes per month.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Does EnviousWispr work offline?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">Transcription runs entirely on-device and works without internet. AI polish requires an LLM; you can use a local model for fully offline operation or bring your own API key for a cloud provider.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Will my audio be used for training?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">No. Your audio is transcribed on your Mac and never leaves it. Dictation audio is cleared after processing, and meeting audio stays on your Mac until you delete it. Envious Labs never receives it, so it cannot be used for anything else.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Can I use both Otter.ai and EnviousWispr?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">Yes. They do not conflict. You can keep Otter for meetings your team shares and searches, and use EnviousWispr for dictation and for meetings you want kept on your own Mac.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">What Mac do I need?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">Any Mac with Apple Silicon (M1 or later) running macOS 14 Sonoma or newer. The Neural Engine and GPU on Apple Silicon are what make on-device transcription fast.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Is EnviousWispr open source?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">Open source under the GNU General Public License v3 (GPLv3), an OSI-approved license. You can read, build, inspect, and contribute to every line of code on GitHub. Contributions are welcome.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Does Otter.ai work as a dictation tool?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">Otter.ai is designed for meeting transcription, not for typing by voice into other apps. It records conversations and produces transcripts inside its own interface. To get that text into an email or document, you need to copy and paste. EnviousWispr is the opposite: it pastes text directly into whatever app you are using, with no intermediate step.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Can Otter.ai transcribe on-device?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">No. Otter.ai is cloud-only. All audio is uploaded to their servers for transcription, speaker identification, and AI processing. There is no offline or on-device mode. EnviousWispr runs entirely on your Mac's Apple Silicon chip and works without internet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Is Otter.ai free?</div>
        <p class="faq-a">Otter has a free tier with 300 minutes per month and a 30-minute per-conversation limit. Beyond that, Pro is $8.33/month billed annually ($16.99 monthly) with 1,200 minutes a month, and Business is $19.99/month billed annually ($30 monthly). EnviousWispr is completely free with no usage limits, no subscription tiers, and no account required.</p>
